o  it you're going to have to separate  those bands anyway so that's something  that's in the instruction manuals for  these lights so do a little tip or trick  right there for you as well okay um what  else to talk about in terms of the  system in terms of the speeds speeds are  interesting because  speeds are never what they put on the  box never  never 11 000 mbps it's like 10  gpps  i mean i don't work on the starship  enterprise i don't have speeds like that  we'll never see them probably in the  next couple years who knows but i have  one in gpps so what are my speeds like  realistically if i'm right next to the  main node which is next to my modem i'm  around 7 to 750  mbps in terms of speed right next to it  now here's the thing with mesh systems  whenever you put a node to it you know  the second node or the third node et  cetera et cetera expect your speed  speeds to drop anywhere from 40 to 50  percent  yes 40 to 50 percent  this one i dropped about 25 to 30  so i went from 700  to about 450 almost 500 on the second  node which is impressive for me  very impressive my user experience for  the past couple weeks has been good no  drop signals all my devices will say  most of my devices connect most of them  do  um i found that 5g.1 is better than 5g.2  for the devices i have and these are all  the latest iphones macbook pros  uh  ipads other products in that nature  they all work better on 5g.1 i don't  know maybe 5g.2 is more future-proofed  and  products aren't developed for it yet but  as it stands right now if you do get  this try 5g.1 as your de facto and i  think you'll be very happy with the  speeds you get out of it as i mentioned  not all my products connect to this  wi-fi system that good why  interesting um  as i mentioned some of these wi-fi  lighting systems case in point i have  the terabolt display cabinet behind me  right and these are actually  lights that connect to wi-fi system so i  connect it to an app on my phone and i  can change the 